# tak-uas-live — UAS gimbal feed over the COMPRESSED edge leg.
#
# The perception node (hephaestus) encodes manto's ANNOTATED feed to
# H.264 MPEG-TS on tcp :5602 (one encode, teed with the nerv-gcs RFC4571
# stream — see docs/TAK-UAS-VIDEO.md and ~/bin/manto-broadcast.sh).  The
# Mac tunnels that TCP stream and decodes it locally with tools/vdec
# (ffmpeg), served through vid9p, so the WAN carries compressed H.264
# instead of raw ~41 MB/s I420.  vid9p serves the decoded stream at
# /tmp/vision/0.
#
#   demo-tak.sh          # wires the tunnel + vid9p/vdec mount + launch
#
# The heavier raw-I420-direct-9P path is demo-tak-raw.sh + tak-uas.

layout vsplit 100 0

top video-pane /tmp/vision/0
